speechtext:
Item agreed to.
Customs tariff-462. Blowers of iron or steel of a class or kind not made in Canada, for use in the smelting of ores, or in reduction, separation or refining of metals, ores or minerals; rotary kilns, revolving roasters and furnaces of metal of a class or kind not made in Canada, designed for roasting ore, mineral, rock or clay; furnace slag trucks and slag pots of a class or kind not made in Canada, and integral parts of all machinery mentioned in this item:	British preferential tariff, free;
intermediate tariff, free; general tariff, free.

Before we carry any of
these items, I think there are a few points of information that should be given on each item. We have appointed a tariff board, and most of us agree that an advisory tariff board is probably a good thing because it can study the questions more thoroughly than we have time to do as members of this house. In view of that it seems to me that on each of these items we should be told (1) if the item has been before the board; (2) what is the report of the board on that item, and what is their recommendation in the matter;
(3)	what were the imports and the revenues associated therewith in the previous year;
(4)	what change will it make in the revenues of the country.
